TI  - Wikidata as a knowledge graph for the life sciences.
LID - 10.7554/eLife.52614 [doi]
LID - e52614
AB  - Wikidata is a community-maintained knowledge base that has been assembled from 
      repositories in the fields of genomics, proteomics, genetic variants, pathways, 
      chemical compounds, and diseases, and that adheres to the FAIR principles of 
      findability, accessibility, interoperability and reusability. Here we describe 
      the breadth and depth of the biomedical knowledge contained within Wikidata, and 
      discuss the open-source tools we have built to add information to Wikidata and to 
      synchronize it with source databases. We also demonstrate several use cases for 
      Wikidata, including the crowdsourced curation of biomedical ontologies, 
      phenotype-based diagnosis of disease, and drug repurposing.
